11. HOSTILE CREATURE SYSTEM — PARAMETRIC MOB AI
============================================================

Introduce hostile creatures that make traversal
more interesting and demanding.

The term parametric refers to deterministic movement
defined using parameters and trajectories.

Use predictable mathematical movement functions
rather than arbitrary random wandering.

Possible trajectory functions:

- Sine-wave patrol.
- Cosine patrol.
- Bezier curves.
- Elliptical flight.
- Waypoint loops.
- Controlled pursuit.
- Deterministic state-based movement.

Create at least THREE distinct hostile archetypes.

ENEMY A — HUSHED STALKER

Ground-based hostile creature.

Behavior:
- Patrol.
- Detect Nima within a defined range.
- Enter alert state.
- Telegraph a short charge.
- Charge along a controlled path.
- Recover.
- Return to patrol.

ENEMY B — GLOOM MOTH

Flying hostile creature.

Behavior:
- Follows a parametric flying route.
- Detects Nima.
- Changes direction visibly.
- Telegraphs a swoop.
- Performs a controlled attack trajectory.
- Recovers and returns to patrol.

ENEMY C — ROOTBOUND SENTINEL

Stationary or semi-stationary creature.

Behavior:
- Guards a defined area.
- Telegraphs root-based attacks.
- Produces predictable ground hazards.
- Has clear recovery periods.
- Reacts to Wake.

Add additional types where appropriate.

AI STATE SYSTEM:

Every hostile creature should have states such as:

IDLE
PATROL
ALERT
TELEGRAPH
ATTACK
RECOVER
STUNNED
DEFEATED_OR_RETREATED

Movement must be deterministic and testable.

HOSTILE CREATURE FAIRNESS:

- Visible attack telegraphs.
- Readable movement.
- Fair collision bounds.
- Predictable behavior.
- No unavoidable spawn attacks.
